    "result": "Perfect! Both issues have been fixed and all tests are now passing. Here's what was wrong and how I fixed it:\n\n## Issues Fixed\n\n1. **Missing named exports in `packages/frai-core/src/finetune/index.js`**\n   - The test was trying to import `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export, but it was only available in the default export\n   - **Fix**: Added named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS`\n\n2. **Toxicity metric receiving wrong parameter in `packages/frai-core/src/eval/metrics.js`**\n   - The `runEvaluations` function passes `(outputs, references)` to all metrics, but `toxicityMetric` was expecting `(outputs, bannedTerms)`\n   - This caused references to be treated as banned terms, incorrectly flagging safe text\n   - **Fix**: Changed `toxicityMetric` signature to accept `(outputs, references)` and ignore the references parameter, always using `defaultBannedTerms`\n\n## Test Results\n\u2705 All test files passing: **8/8**  \n\u2705 All tests passing: **28/28**\n\nThe fixes maintain backward compatibility\u2014the constants remain accessible through the default export, and the toxicity metric now works correctly with the evaluation harness.",
